  <section id="purpose" class="doc-section">
    <h2>What the CAM kernel is</h2>
    <p>The CAM kernel in <code>packages/core/src/cam/kernel</code> (20 source files, about 5 260 lines) takes a revisioned manufacturing job to machine NC plus evidence about that NC. It chooses cutters and cutting data, plans operations from the CAD features, runs the strategies, posts G-code, replays the NC independently against volumetric stock, and checks the motion of the tool assembly for collisions. Its algorithm identity is <code>cadcamfun-cam-kernel@1</code>.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>materials</td><td>workpiece grades with their machinability data</td></tr>
        <tr><td>cutters</td><td>tool assemblies and the default library (70 cutters)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>cutting-data</td><td>speeds, feeds, depths, load and deflection for a cutter in a material</td></tr>
        <tr><td>planner</td><td>CAD features → ordered operations with their cutters</td></tr>
        <tr><td>execute</td><td>prepare / run: strategies, post, independent NC replay, stock lineage, claims and release level</td></tr>
        <tr><td>kinematics, head</td><td>trunnion table (AC / BC) and tilting head (B about Y)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>assembly</td><td>the 3D tool assembly (cutting zone, shank, holder) as a profile and its solid of revolution</td></tr>
        <tr><td>collision</td><td>continuous check of a joint move: certified clear, collision or unresolved</td></tr>
        <tr><td>motion</td><td>simultaneous five-axis: locations → table poses, each move split and checked</td></tr>
        <tr><td>stock</td><td>volumetric stock as voxels with a remaining-volume bracket</td></tr>
        <tr><td>machine-clearance</td><td>holder and shank against the table over every NC move</td></tr>
        <tr><td>convex</td><td>exact distance between convex hulls (GJK)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
