  <section id="stock" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Voxel stock and the remaining-volume bracket</h2>
    <p>Stock is a voxel grid. After a set of moves each voxel is material, <em>removed sure</em> (its whole cube lay inside the cutter at some sampled position) or <em>removed possible</em> (its cube came within the cutter&apos;s expansion: half a diagonal plus half the sample spacing). The remaining volume is therefore a bracket: material not possibly removed is definitely left, material not surely removed may be left. A voxel is never called removed without a sampled cutter covering it. Tilted tools carry their axis per tip point, so five-axis sweeps use the same two tests.</p>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="stock.ts">
{"export const voxelStock: (min: Vec3, max: Vec3, voxel: number) => VoxelStock   // sample step = voxel / 2\nexport const removeTipPath: (stock: VoxelStock, cutter: Cutter, path: ReadonlyArray<Vec3>, axes?: ReadonlyArray<Vec3>) => void\nexport const remainingVolume: (stock: VoxelStock) => { lower: number; upper: number }"}
    </DocCode>
    <DocCode language="ts" title="Slot and ring 3 mm deep with flat-6 — real output">
{"const s = voxelStock({ x: 0, y: 0, z: -10 }, { x: 40, y: 30, z: 0 }, 0.5)\n// 80 \u00d7 60 \u00d7 20 = 96 000 voxels, step 0.25\nremoveTipPath(s, flat6, path)          // slot y = 15, x 8\u219232, then the ring 8..32 \u00d7 8..22, all at z \u22123\nremainingVolume(s)                     // {\u0022lower\u0022:9749.5,\u0022upper\u0022:10740}   124 ms\n// stock 12 000 mm\u00b3: between 1 260 and 2 250.5 mm\u00b3 removed"}
